WEBVTT

00:00:03.567 --> 00:00:08.389
McKinsey finds that 88 percent
of organizations now use AI.

00:00:08.429 --> 00:00:11.939
Only 39 percent report any impact on EBIT.

00:00:11.979 --> 00:00:15.860
And BCG finds that 5 percent
create value at scale.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:19.417
Using AI has become common.
Repeating it has not.

00:00:19.833 --> 00:00:23.563
The Adoption Tree Model is an
operating model for that gap.

00:00:23.603 --> 00:00:29.114
It takes an organization from one working
AI use case to the ability to repeat it.

00:00:29.533 --> 00:00:30.775
Read it as a tree.

00:00:30.815 --> 00:00:34.092
The branches are the use
cases people see and use.

00:00:34.132 --> 00:00:38.131
The roots are six blocks of
capability the organization keeps.

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:41.320
And the trunk is the Adoption Office: a small,

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:44.272
jointly staffed team, temporary by design.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:49.335
The office takes each use case through
six gates, from mandate to transfer.

00:00:49.375 --> 00:00:53.562
Each gate is a decision with a
named owner and minimum evidence.

00:00:53.602 --> 00:00:57.193
A reference wave takes
twenty-four weeks of working time.

00:00:57.233 --> 00:01:01.183
In a regulated enterprise, plan
nine to twelve months elapsed.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:04.657
What sets the model apart
happens after go-live.

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:07.656
Every live use case leaves something behind:

00:01:07.696 --> 00:01:10.968
approved data, a tested
control, trained people.

00:01:11.008 --> 00:01:15.235
That flows back into the roots, so the
next use case starts further ahead.

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:20.424
The foundation enables the use case. The
use case makes the foundation stronger.

00:01:20.464 --> 00:01:24.898
And the office is built to leave:
dependency is designed to decline,

00:01:24.938 --> 00:01:27.175
and trained Adoption Coaches stay.

00:01:27.633 --> 00:01:31.612
The Adoption Tree Model. Build
AI capability that stays.

00:01:31.652 --> 00:01:34.646
Get the white paper at adoptiontree.ai.
